1041	\section{Conditionally linear functions and distributions}
1042	% Paper subsection label sec:cl kept for cross-reference fidelity.
1043	\label{sec:cl}
1044	
1045	Conditionally linear functions specify the question distributions of the games considered in the following chapters in a form that can be ``introspected''. Intuitively, a conditionally linear function takes as input an element $x \in V = \F^n$ and applies linear maps $L_j$ sequentially to $x^{V_j}$, where $V_1, V_2, \dots$ is a sequence of complementary register subspaces such that both the linear map $L_j$ and the subspace $V_j$, for $j \ge 2$, may depend on the values taken by the previous linear maps $L_1(x^{V_1})$, $L_2(x^{V_2})$, and so on.
1046	
1047	Throughout this section $V$ denotes the linear space $\F^n$ for some integer $n \ge 0$, and all the distinguished subspaces of $V$ are register subspaces (Definition~\ref{def:register-subspace}). If $V_1, V_2, \dots, V_\ell$ are fixed subspaces of $V$ and $k \in \{1, 2, \dots, \ell\}$, we use the subscript range notation
1048	\[
1049		V_{<k} = \bigoplus_{j\,:\,1 \le j < k} V_j\,, \qquad V_{>k} = \bigoplus_{j\,:\,\ell \ge j > k} V_j\,,
1050	\]
1051	and $V_{\le k}$, $V_{\ge k}$ are understood to be $V_{<k+1}$ and $V_{>k-1}$, respectively. For a register subspace $V'$ of $V$, the symbol $x^{V'}$ denotes the projection of $x$ onto $V'$ parallel to the complementary register subspace (Definition~\ref{def:complementary}). Moreover, if $F \colon V' \to V'$ is a function and $x \in V$, we write $x^F$ for $F(x^{V'})$; for example, in the following definition $x^{L_1}$ is shorthand for $L_1(x^{V_1})$.
1052	
1053	\begin{definition}[Conditionally linear functions]\label{def:cl-func}
1054		\uses{def:register-subspace, def:complementary}
1055		Let $V$ be $\F^n$ for some $n \ge 0$. For all integers $\ell \ge 0$ the collection of \emph{$\ell$-level conditionally linear functions} (implicitly, \emph{on $V$}) is defined inductively as follows.
1056		\begin{enumerate}
1057			\item There is a single $0$-level conditionally linear function, which is the $0$ function on $V$.
1058			\item Let $\ell \ge 1$ and suppose the collection of $(\ell-1)$-level conditionally linear functions has been defined. The collection of $\ell$-level conditionally linear functions on $V$ consists of all functions $L$ on $V$ that can be expressed in the following form: there exist complementary register subspaces $V_1$ and $V_{>1}$ of $V$, a linear function $L_1$ on $V_1$, and, for all $v \in L_1(V_1)$, an $(\ell-1)$-level conditionally linear function $L_{>1,\,v}$ on $V_{>1}$, such that for all $x \in V$,
1059			\[
1060				L(x) = x^{L_1} + L_{>1,\,x^{L_1}}(x^{V_{>1}})\,.

300	
