302		The implication above does not extend to submeasurements. For example, if
303		$A_a^x=0$ for all $a$, then $A_a^x \ot I \simeq_0 I \ot B_a^x$, but
304		\[
305			\E_{\bx} \sum_a \lVert (A^{\bx}_a \ot I - I \ot B^{\bx}_a)\ket{\psi} \rVert^2
306			= \E_{\bx} \sum_a \lVert (I \ot B^{\bx}_a)\ket{\psi} \rVert^2,
307		\]
308		which is nonzero unless $(I \ot B_a^x)\ket{\psi}=0$ for all $x$ and $a$.
309	\end{remark}
